{P. Keres evaluated the diagrammed position as drawn, and numerous authors
reproduced this judgment. Yet N. Elkies, an Israeli endgame study composer,
discovered a subtle winning method many years later. Its idea can be briefly
described as follows: the king retreats to g4, the rook goes to b5 or d5,
denying the bishop important squares. Thereafter, depending on the bishop's
position, the white king breaks through to f6 or h6, while if the bishop is on
f8 or g7, the advance g5-g6 is very strong.} 1. Rb3 $1 (1. Kg4 $6 {is
inaccurate:} Bc1 $1 {/\ h6} 2. Kf5 Bd2 (2... h6 $2 3. Kg6 $1 $18) 3. Rb2 (3.
Rb3 Kg7) 3... Be3 (3... Bc1 4. Rb8+ Kg7 5. Rb7+ Kg8 6. Kf6) 4. Rb3 Bd4) 1...
Bd6 (1... Bf8 {loses rapidly:} 2. Rb8 Kg7 3. Rb7+ Kg8 4. g6) ({If} 1... Bc5 2.
Kg4 Bd6 {then} 3. Rb5 Bc7 4. Rd5 $1 {and the king is ready for a march.}) 2.
Kg4 Bf8 $5 (2... Bc5 {is met with} 3. Rb5 $1 {and the bishop cannot prevent an
invasion by the king. For example:} Bf8 (3... Bd4 4. Kh5 {/\ Rb8+, Rb7+, Kh6}
Bg7 5. g6 h6 6. Rb8+ Bf8 7. Rxf8+ Kxf8 8. Kxh6) (3... Bd6 4. Kf5 Bc7 5. Rd5 $1
Bb6 (5... Bg3 6. Kf6) 6. Kf6 Bc7 7. Rd7 Ba5 8. Rg7+ $1 Kh8 9. Kf7 $18) (3...
Ba3 4. Kf5) 4. Kf5 h6 (4... Bg7 5. g6 $1 h6 6. Rb8+ Bf8 7. Kf6) (4... Be7 5.
Rb8+ Kf7 6. Rb7 {/\ Kg4-h5-h6}) 5. g6 (5. gxh6 Kh7 6. Rb6 Bxh6 7. Rb7+ $18 {is
also good.}) 5... Be7 (5... Bd6 6. Kf6) 6. Rb8+ Kg7 7. Rb7) 3. Kf5 $1 ({White
has no time for previously planned} 3. Rb5 $2 {because after} h6 $1 4. g6 Bd6 {
he cannot prevent the bishop transfer to the diagonal c1-h6 that saves Black:}
5. Kf5 Bg3 $1 6. Ra5 Bh4 7. Ra8+ Kg7 8. Ra7+ Kg8 9. g7 Kh7 10. Ke6 ({Nothing
can be achieved with} 10. Rf7 Bg5 11. g8=Q+ Kxg8 12. Kg6 Bd2 13. Rd7 Bg5 $11 {
as well.} (13... Bb4 14. Rd8+ Bf8 15. Rc8 h5 16. Kxh5 Kf7 $11)) 10... Kg8 $11)
3... Bc5 4. Rd3 $1 Bb4 ({If} 4... Be7 {then} 5. Rc3 $1 Bb4 6. Rc8+ Kf7 7. Rc7+
Be7 (7... Kg8 8. Kf6) 8. Kg4 $18 {and Kh5-h6 is irresistible.}) 5. Kf6 Ba5 6.
Rb3 Bd8+ (6... Bc7 7. Rb5 Bd8+ 8. Ke6 $1 Kg7 9. Kd7) 7. Kf5 Ba5 (7... Bc7 8.
Rb5) 8. Kg4 Bc7 9. Rb5 $1 Bd6 10. Kf5 Bc7 11. Rd5 $18 1-0

