1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 Ne7 5. a3 Bxc3+ 6. bxc3 b6 7. Qg4 Kf8 (7...
Ng6 8. h4 h5 9. Qg3) 8. h4 c5 9. h5 h6 10. Rh3 Qc7 (10... Ba6 11. Bxa6 (11. Ne2
Qd7 12. Rf3 Nf5 13. Qf4 cxd4 14. cxd4 Nc6 15. c3 Na5 16. Rb1 Rc8 17. g4 $16 {
Bolado Saez,S-Garcia Carbo,M/Padron 2004}) 11... Nxa6 12. Qe2 Qc8 13. Bd2 cxd4
14. cxd4 Qc4 $11 {Pirttimaki,T-Hansen,C/Uzhgorod 1988}) 11. Bd2 $5 {Very good
and natural move which appears to be a novelty.} (11. Kd1 Nbc6 12. Qf4 Bd7 13.
Rf3 Be8 14. g4 cxd4 15. cxd4 b5 16. Bd3 Nd8 17. Ne2 $16 {Khlusevich,S-Sliwa,B/
Russia 1993}) (11. Rf3 cxd4 12. Qf4 Nf5 13. Ne2 Ba6 14. cxd4 Nc6 15. Bb2 Kg8
16. g4 Nh4 17. Rc3 $14 {Ginzburg,M-Rodriguez,A/Buenos Aires 1994}) (11. Qd1 Ba6
12. g4 Bxf1 13. Kxf1 Nbc6 14. Kg2 Ke8 15. Ne2 cxd4 16. cxd4 Na5 $13 {Senff,
M-Bukal,V/Paks 1997}) 11... Ba6 ({Of course not} 11... cxd4 12. cxd4 Qxc2 $4
13. Rc1 $18) 12. Rf3 cxd4 13. cxd4 Bxf1 14. Kxf1 Nbc6 $2 {A blunder which
could end the game right after the opening!} (14... Kg8) 15. Bb4 $2 {Amazingly
white misses the chance to win a pawn and most probably the game!} (15. Qxe6
Nd8 16. Qd6 Qxc2 17. Bb4 $18) 15... Kg8 {After this move thing "get back to
normal".} 16. Qf4 {After missing the chance to win after blck's blunder white
has got to win the game again!} Nf5 17. Ne2 a5 18. Bd6 (18. Bd2 Rf8 19. Rb1 Kh7
20. Rfb3 Rhg8 21. Rxb6 Nb4 22. Rb5 Qxc2 23. Rc1 Qd3 24. Rxa5 Nc2 $132) 18...
Qa7 19. g4 Nxd6 20. exd6 f6 $6 {Dubious decision after which white gets very
comfortable advantage due to the control over the very crucial square b5.} (
20... b5 $142 $5) 21. Rb1 Kf7 22. Nc3 Rhd8 23. Nb5 $16 Qd7 24. g5 hxg5 25. Qxg5
{[%cal Gh5h6]} Rh8 26. Qg6+ Kg8 27. Rg3 Rf8 28. c4 $6 (28. h6 Rf7 29. Nc7 Nxd4
30. Rxb6 $18) 28... dxc4 29. Rc1 Rh7 30. h6 Rf7 31. Rxc4 f5 (31... e5 32. d5
Nd8 33. a4 $18) 32. a4 $1 {Protecting the knight.} f4 33. Rg1 e5 34. d5 Qh3+
35. Ke1 Rxh6 36. Qg4 $2 (36. Qxh6 $1 Qxh6 37. dxc6 Qe6 38. Rc3 Rf8 39. d7 $18)
36... Qxg4 37. Rxg4 Na7 $2 {Losing on the spot, while ater correct} (37... Nb8
38. Rc8+ Rf8 39. Rc7 Rf7 $14 {the outcome of the game is far from being clear.}
) 38. Nxa7 $18 Rxd6 (38... Rxa7 39. Rc8+ Kh7 40. Rc7 Ra8 41. Rgxg7+ Kh8 42. d7
$18) 39. Rc8+ Kh7 40. Nc6 Rxd5 41. Re8 f3 42. Nxe5 Rf6 43. Re7 1-0

