1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. Nf3 O-O 6. Be2 e5 7. O-O Nc6 8. d5
Ne7 9. b4 Ne8 ({Nowadays} 9... Nh5 {is much more popular.}) 10. Bd2 (10. c5 $1
{Postny: I expected} f5 {Postny: 'after which I intended to play'} (10... Kh8 {
A rare move. Black is moving his king to a safer square. Also, freeing the
g8-square for a possible knight transfer, since the knight often appears to be
misplaced on e7.} 11. Ba3 $6 {A logical move at first sight, eyeing the Pd6 as
a potential weakness. However, the bishop on a3 obstructs the Pa2, this makes
White's queenside play less effective. The move Bc1-a3 should be played after
a2-a4.} (11. a4 f5 (11... Ng8 12. a5 Qe7 13. c6 f5 14. cxb7 Bxb7 15. Nd2 a6 16.
b5 $14 {1-0 Garcia Ilundain,D (2435)-Hebden,M (2500)/Candas 1992/TD (58)}) 12.
Ng5 ({The logical} 12. a5 {worth considering as well.}) 12... h6 13. Ne6 Bxe6
14. dxe6 fxe4 15. cxd6 Nxd6 16. b5 Qc8 17. Nd5 Re8 18. Bg4 Ndf5 19. Ba3 Nxd5
20. Qxd5 c6 21. Qxe4 Qxe6 22. bxc6 Qxc6 23. Bxf5 gxf5 24. Qxf5 Qxa4 25. Qf7 $44
{1/2-1/2 Gligoric,S (2600)-Evans,L (2550)/Amsterdam 1971/MCL (57)}) (11. Nd2 f5
12. a4 Bh6 $6 (12... Nf6 $142) 13. Ba3 Bxd2 14. Qxd2 f4 15. b5 g5 16. Rfc1 Ng6
17. Bf1 Nh4 18. b6 axb6 19. cxd6 cxd6 20. Nb5 g4 21. Qc3 Rf6 22. Nc7 Nxc7 23.
Qxc7 Qf8 24. Rc3 $16 {1-0 Petkov,V (2529)-Krstic,U (2350)/Zadar 2005/CBM 109
ext (49)}) 11... Ng8 $6 {Transfering the misplaced knight to better pastures.
Meanwhile, the knight on e8 remains to protect the Pd6. Still, I have a
feeling that this plan is too slow.} (11... f5 12. Nd2 (12. Ng5 $2 Nxd5 $15 {
[%csl Rg5][%cal Gd8g5] Another drawback of 11.Ba3 is clear now, White lost
control over g5 square.}) 12... fxe4 13. Ndxe4 Nf5 {occupying the d4-square
was another possibility with reasonable counterplay for Black.}) 12. b5 f5 13.
Qb3 {With the idea of breaking through by b5-b6.} (13. Nd2 Nh6 $6 (13... Ngf6
$142) 14. Nc4 b6 15. cxd6 cxd6 16. Bb4 f4 17. a4 Rb8 18. a5 $16 {1-0 Golod,V 
(2568)-Vinck,M/Vlissingen 1999/EXT 2000 (27)}) 13... b6 $1 14. cxd6 cxd6 15.
Nd2 ({I considered also} 15. Bb4 {[%cal Ga2a4,Ga4a5] but, I decided that it
was more important to put a pressure onthe Pd6 as soon as possible.}) 15...
Ngf6 16. Nc4 Bb7 {Unfortunately, my Pd5 is also a target.} (16... fxe4 17. Bb4
$1 {[%csl Rd6][%cal Gb3a3]} (17. Qb4 $6 Bb7 18. Nxd6 Nxd6 19. Qxd6 Rc8 $15 {
[%csl Rc3,Rd5]}) 17... Bb7 18. Nd2 Nd7 (18... Nc7 19. Bc4 $14) 19. Ncxe4 Nc5
20. Bxc5 bxc5 21. a4 Nf6 22. Bc4 $14) (16... Nxe4 17. Nxe4 fxe4 18. Qb4 {[%csl
Rd6]} Rf6 19. Nd2 $14) 17. Rad1 ({After} 17. f3 $6 {I didn't like} Nh5 {and I
have to either allow my opponent's knight to be established on f4, or to
weaken my king's residence by g2-g3.}) 17... fxe4 18. Nd2 e3 $1 $132 {Correct.
This move creates a weakness in White's camp and does not allow the white
knight to be established on the dominant e4-square.} (18... Nd7 19. Ncxe4 Nc5
20. Bxc5 bxc5 21. Nc4 $16) 19. fxe3 Bh6 {[%csl Re3]} 20. Nc4 Rc8 21. Kh1 Rc7 {
Intending to double rooks along the f-file, and also freeing the c8-square for
a possible transfer of the bishop.} 22. Bb4 Bc8 23. h3 {It is important to
cover the g4-square.} (23. Qa3 $2 Bg4 24. Qb2 (24. Nxd6 $2 Nxd6 25. Bxd6 Rxc3
26. Qxc3 Qxd6 $19) 24... Rxc4 25. Bxc4 Bxd1 26. Nxd1 Nc7 $132) 23... Bf5 24.
Rf2 $1 {I've copied the idea from my opponent, doubling rooks along the f-file.
} Rcf7 (24... Ne4 25. Nxe4 Bxe4 26. Rxf8+ Bxf8 27. Rf1 Bh6 {[%csl Rd5]} 28. Nd2
Bc2 29. Qa3 $16 {[%csl Rd6,Ge6][%cal Gd2c4,Ge2g4,Gg4e6]}) 25. Rdf1 {Again,
Qb3-a3 was bad. The position is full of tactics; I had to be careful not to
come under a dangerous attack.} (25. Qa3 $2 Ne4 $1 26. Nxe4 Bxe4 27. Rxf7 Rxf7
28. Nxd6 (28. Bxd6 Qh4 29. Bg4 Rf2 $1 30. Bxe5+ Bg7 31. Rg1 h5 $1 32. Bxg7+
Nxg7 33. Nd6 Bxg2+ $1 34. Rxg2 Rf1+ 35. Rg1 Rf3 $1 $19) 28... Nxd6 29. Bxd6 Qh4
30. Bxe5+ Bg7 31. Bxg7+ Kxg7 32. Qc3+ Kh6 33. Kh2 Rf2 34. Bf1 Qg5 35. Rd2 Rxf1
$19) 25... Qd7 {[%csl Rh3]} 26. Kh2 Ne4 $2 (26... Bg5 27. Qa3 Bh4 28. Bxd6 (28.
Rxf5 $6 gxf5 29. Bxd6 Rg8 30. Bxe5 Rfg7 $13) 28... Nxd6 29. Nxd6 Bxf2 30. Rxf2
{and after gaining the exchange back, White will be a pawn up.}) (26... Kg8 $1
{was still playable for Black. The king defends both rooks, therefore the
knight move to e4 would become possible on the next move. For example:} 27. Qa3
Ne4 28. Nxe4 Bxe4 29. Rxf7 Rxf7 30. Nxd6 Rxf1 31. Bxf1 Nxd6 32. Bxd6 Qf7 33.
Kg1 Qxd5 $11) 27. Nxe4 $2 {Being in time-pressure, I played this move quickly,
missing a nice tactical opportunity to win outright.} (27. Nxe5 $1 dxe5 (27...
Nxf2 28. Nxd7 Bxd7 29. Nd1 $18) 28. Nxe4 Bxe4 29. Bxf8 $18) 27... Bxe4 28. Rxf7
Rxf7 29. Nd2 Rxf1 30. Bxf1 Qf5 $2 (30... Nf6 31. Qa3 (31. Nxe4 Nxe4 {followed
by 32...Nc5, equalising.}) 31... Bxd5 32. Bxd6 Qe6 $11) 31. Qc4 Bxe3 $4 {Just
blundering away a piece. However, Black's position was already very difficult.}
(31... Nf6 32. Nxe4 Nxe4 (32... Qxe4 33. Bxd6 Qxe3 34. g3 Qe1 35. Qc8+ Ng8 36.
Bg2 $18) 33. Bd3 Bf4+ $8 34. exf4 Qxf4+ 35. Kg1 Qe3+ 36. Kh1 Nf2+ (36... Qxd3
37. Qxd3 Nf2+ 38. Kh2 Nxd3 39. Bxd6 {[%csl Ra7,Rb6][%cal Gd6b8] with a won
endgame.}) 37. Kh2 Nxd3 38. Bxd6 $16) 32. Nxe4 {Probably, my opponent simply
overlooked that my queen covers both Ne4 and Bf1. The rest was easy.} Bd4 33.
Qe2 Qf4+ 34. g3 Qc1 35. Nxd6 Nf6 36. Bd2 Qa3 37. Nf7+ Kg7 38. Ng5 Nh5 39. Qf3 {
1-0 Postny,E (2599)-Visser,Y (2470)/Hoogeveen 2007/CBM 121/[Postny]}) 11. Ng5 {
Postny: 'This is one of the well-known theoretical lines.'} Nf6 12. f3 Kh8 13.
Be3 Bh6 14. Nf7+ Rxf7 15. Bxh6 f4 16. Rc1 Neg8 17. Bg5 Rg7 $146 (17... h6) 18.
g4 h5 19. h3 Rh7 20. Kg2 Bd7 21. Rh1 Rc8 22. Qg1 Ra8 23. a4 Qf8 24. a5 Nh6 25.
Bh4 g5 26. Bf2 a6 27. Kf1 {1/2-1/2 Bacrot,E (2675)-Radjabov,T (2670)/Tripolis
2004/Informador 91}) 10... f5 11. Ng5 (11. Be3 f4 12. Bd2 h6 13. c5 Rf7 14. Ne1
Nf6 15. Bc4 Kh8 16. f3 g5 17. g4 fxg3 18. hxg3 Ng6 19. Kg2 Qe7 20. cxd6 cxd6
21. Rh1 Kh7 22. Bxg5 Qc7 23. Qb3 Qb6 24. Na4 Qc7 25. Nc3 Bd7 26. Nb5 Qb6 27.
Be3 Qd8 28. Nxd6 Bh3+ 29. Rxh3 Qxd6 30. Bc5 Qd7 31. a4 b6 32. Bb5 Qc7 33. Be3
Qd6 34. Rc1 Rc7 35. Rxc7 Qxc7 36. Bc6 Rc8 37. Rh1 Qf7 38. b5 Ne7 39. Qb2 Rf8
40. Qd2 Rd8 41. Bxh6 Kg8 42. Bxg7 Qxg7 43. Qh6 {1-0 Savina,A-Jussupow,E/
Chalkidiki 2001/EXT 2002}) (11. Qb3 h6 (11... Nf6 12. exf5 (12. c5 h6 13. Qc4
fxe4 14. Nxe4 Nfxd5 15. Rad1 Be6 16. cxd6 cxd6 17. Qb5 b6 18. Qa4 Kh8 19. b5
Qd7 20. Qa3 Rad8 21. Bc1 Nc8 22. Nh4 Qf7 23. Qg3 Nde7 24. f4 Bf5 25. fxe5 dxe5
